        commonIssues: [ "Catastrophic Oil Consumption: The defining flaw of the EA888 Gen 2. The factory piston oil scraper rings are too thin and lack drainage holes. They clog with carbon, causing the engine to burn massive amounts of oil (up to 1L per 500km).", "Timing Chain Tensioner Failure: The original spring-loaded chain tensioner teeth shear off, causing the chain to skip and pistons to smash the valves. Must be upgraded to the revised ratchet style.", "Water Pump & Thermostat Housing Leaks: The entire water pump assembly is made of plastic and bolts to the side of the engine block. It warps from heat cycling and constantly leaks coolant.", "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Due to direct injection, oil vapor from the PCV system bakes onto the intake valves, forming rock-hard carbon that severely restricts airflow and causes misfires.", "PCV Valve Failure: The crankcase ventilation diaphragm tears, causing a massive internal vacuum leak, a loud whistling noise, and exacerbating the oil consumption issue.", "Ignition Coil Pack Failure: The COP units fail predictably under the high cylinder pressures of direct injection, causing violent misfires under load." ],
        vulnerabilities: [ "Instant Valvetrain Destruction - If the un-revised timing chain tensioner fails on startup, the engine will skip timing and bend all 16 valves, requiring a €2000+ cylinder head rebuild.", "Piston Ring Clogging - The inherent design of the scraper rings means they will eventually fail. The only permanent fix is a complete engine rebuild with modified pistons and wider rings.", "Balance Shaft Seizure - The balance shafts are driven by a secondary chain. If the fine mesh screens inside the shafts clog with debris, the bearings seize, locking the engine up completely.", "Rear Main Seal Blowout - A failed PCV valve can over-pressurize the crankcase, completely blowing out the rear main seal between the engine and transmission, requiring gearbox removal to fix.", "Turbocharger Wastegate Rattle - The internal wastegate flapper arm wears loose, causing a rattling noise on deceleration and an inability to hold target boost." ],
        oemPlusUpgrades: [ { name: "Revised Timing Chain Tensioner (06K)", description: "Replacing the ticking-time-bomb factory tensioner with the latest 'K' revision ratchet-style tensioner.", benefit: "Absolutely mandatory. Permanently prevents the timing chain from skipping and destroying the engine." }, { name: "Pierburg 'Rev D' Diverter Valve", description: "Replacing the fragile rubber diaphragm diverter valve with the OEM piston-style valve.", benefit: "Eliminates boost leaks caused by torn diaphragms. Bulletproof, maintenance-free, and handles tuned boost levels flawlessly." }, { name: "R8 Ignition Coils", description: "Upgrading to the high-output red ignition coils from the Audi R8.", benefit: "Delivers a much stronger spark, smoothing out the idle, preventing high-RPM misfires, and looking great in the engine bay." }, { name: "Walnut Blasting (Carbon Clean)", description: "Physically blasting the intake valves with crushed walnut shells to remove carbon buildup.", benefit: "Restores lost horsepower, fixes cold-start misfires, and allows the direct-injected engine to breathe properly." } ],
